	<body>
		<segment id="1" parent="2" relname="adversative-concession">I do n't know about you ,</segment>
		<segment id="2" parent="149" relname="span">but sooner or later I need a photo .</segment>
		<segment id="3" parent="148" relname="span">As a library web guy , I tend to use a lot of photos .</segment>
		<segment id="4" parent="150" relname="joint-list">Some are for promoting an event .</segment>
		<segment id="5" parent="230" relname="span">Some might be used</segment>
		<segment id="6" parent="5" relname="purpose-goal">to liven up some text .</segment>
		<segment id="7" parent="150" relname="joint-list">A photo might be for a post on Facebook or an email campaign through constant contact .</segment>
		<segment id="8" parent="185" relname="span">The problem is you ca n't just use any photo</segment>
		<segment id="9" parent="8" relname="adversative-concession">or at least you should n't .</segment>
		<segment id="10" parent="231" relname="span">It 's funny ,</segment>
		<segment id="11" parent="10" relname="explanation-justify">if you think about it ,</segment>
		<segment id="12" parent="166" relname="span">that there 's a form of piracy</segment>
		<segment id="13" parent="188" relname="span">totally overlooked by the music industry , the motion picture industry , the software industry , the publishing industry , and any other industry</segment>
		<segment id="14" parent="13" relname="elaboration-attribute">concerned with the , quote , threat of piracy , unquote .</segment>
		<segment id="15" parent="154" relname="span">And that is that you can right click on any image in your web browser</segment>
		<segment id="16" parent="15" relname="causal-result">and have a copy of it for yourself .</segment>
		<segment id="17" parent="172" relname="adversative-concession">Very few people seem to be concerned about this .</segment>
		<segment id="18" parent="232" relname="organization-phatic">I mean ,</segment>
		<segment id="19" parent="232" relname="span">sure , there are workarounds and JavaScript</segment>
		<segment id="20" parent="19" relname="purpose-attribute">to disable right clicking on a website .</segment>
		<segment id="21" parent="22" relname="organization-phatic">The thing is ,</segment>
		<segment id="22" parent="189" relname="span">on any web browser , you can get a screenshot plugin to capture the image on the page .</segment>
		<segment id="23" parent="155" relname="joint-list">You can also use the built in screenshot functions in OS Ten , Windows and some distros of Linux .</segment>
		<segment id="24" parent="155" relname="joint-list">Heck , you can go get some really nice free screenshot apps for all the major operating systems .</segment>
		<segment id="25" parent="26" relname="topic-solutionhood">Right click is disabled ?</segment>
		<segment id="26" parent="156" relname="span">No problem .</segment>
		<segment id="27" parent="234" relname="span">There are 1,000 other ways</segment>
		<segment id="28" parent="27" relname="purpose-attribute">to copy that image .</segment>
		<segment id="29" parent="237" relname="adversative-concession">Copying an image is easy ,</segment>
		<segment id="30" parent="237" relname="same-unit">but</segment>
		<segment id="31" parent="236" relname="same-unit">if you want to stay on the right side of ethics , and ,</segment>
		<segment id="32" parent="33" relname="attribution-positive">I suppose ,</segment>
		<segment id="33" parent="195" relname="span">the law ,</segment>
		<segment id="34" parent="160" relname="span">what you need is an image</segment>
		<segment id="35" parent="192" relname="span">that you 're free to use on your library 's websites</segment>
		<segment id="36" parent="235" relname="span">without the fear</segment>
		<segment id="37" parent="36" relname="elaboration-attribute">of a cease and desist showing up on your director 's desk .</segment>
		<segment id="38" parent="193" relname="elaboration-additional">Thankfully , you have incredible free options available to you .</segment>
		<segment id="39" parent="238" relname="span">This is Cyberpunk Librarian episode 32 :</segment>
		<segment id="40" parent="39" relname="elaboration-additional">Picture This !</segment>
		<segment id="41" parent="198" relname="span">My name is Daniel Messer , your friendly neighborhood Cyberpunk Librarian ,</segment>
		<segment id="42" parent="197" relname="span">welcoming you back to the show</segment>
		<segment id="43" parent="239" relname="joint-list">that is all about exploring the intersection between libraries and technology ,</segment>
		<segment id="44" parent="239" relname="joint-list">and living that high tech , low budget lifestyle .</segment>
		<segment id="45" parent="199" relname="organization-phatic">So hey , my listeners , hello , hello , and welcome .</segment>
		<segment id="46" parent="199" relname="joint-list">Cyberpunk Librarian is back on the air or on the net or on your podcatcher of choice ,</segment>
		<segment id="47" parent="158" relname="span">and we have some interesting updates</segment>
		<segment id="48" parent="159" relname="span">to get to</segment>
		<segment id="49" parent="48" relname="context-circumstance">before diving into the show .</segment>
		<segment id="50" parent="204" relname="span">I promise I 'll be quick ,</segment>
		<segment id="51" parent="161" relname="span">because no one wants to sit through a bunch of boring housekeeping stuff</segment>
		<segment id="52" parent="51" relname="context-circumstance">while waiting for the show to start .</segment>
		<segment id="53" parent="200" relname="span">So hey , I am heading off to the Innovative Users Group ,</segment>
		<segment id="54" parent="203" relname="span">which is also the Polaris Users Group ,</segment>
		<segment id="55" parent="201" relname="span">since Innovative Interfaces Incorporated ,</segment>
		<segment id="56" parent="55" relname="elaboration-attribute">sometimes called Triple - I ,</segment>
		<segment id="57" parent="202" relname="same-unit">bought Polaris ILS last year .</segment>
		<segment id="58" parent="59" relname="causal-cause">I 'm speaking this year ,</segment>
		<segment id="59" parent="207" relname="span">so it 's been crazy trying to get things together .</segment>
		<segment id="60" parent="151" relname="joint-list">Make sure my talk is right ,</segment>
		<segment id="61" parent="151" relname="joint-list">pack my bag ,</segment>
		<segment id="62" parent="241" relname="span">figure out what a desert cyberpunk needs in Minneapolis to survive , and all of that .</segment>
		<segment id="63" parent="240" relname="explanation-evidence">Looking at the weather report ,</segment>
		<segment id="64" parent="65" relname="attribution-positive">I suspect</segment>
		<segment id="65" parent="240" relname="span">I 'm going to need a parka and mukluks ,</segment>
		<segment id="66" parent="243" relname="same-unit">but</segment>
		<segment id="67" parent="244" relname="span">if you happen to be a listener</segment>
		<segment id="68" parent="208" relname="span">heading to the IUG PUG convention ,</segment>
		<segment id="69" parent="68" relname="adversative-concession">whatever you 'd like to call it</segment>
		<segment id="70" parent="246" relname="same-unit">on April 13th , 2015 ,</segment>
		<segment id="71" parent="245" relname="span">hey , tweet me at Bibrarian</segment>
		<segment id="72" parent="152" relname="joint-list">and we could maybe meet up ,</segment>
		<segment id="73" parent="152" relname="joint-list">get some drinks ,</segment>
		<segment id="74" parent="152" relname="joint-list">maybe get some dinner ,</segment>
		<segment id="75" parent="152" relname="joint-list">just say hi .</segment>
		<segment id="76" parent="152" relname="joint-list">Whatever .</segment>
		<segment id="77" parent="152" relname="evaluation-comment">But I would love to see any listeners there .</segment>
		<segment id="78" parent="162" relname="span">And hey , the feedback on episode 30 storytime</segment>
		<segment id="79" parent="78" relname="elaboration-attribute">featuring Skylar and Jessica in Intergalactic Librarian</segment>
		<segment id="80" parent="209" relname="same-unit">was amazing .</segment>
		<segment id="81" parent="163" relname="span">So coming soon from the weirdo</segment>
		<segment id="82" parent="81" relname="elaboration-attribute">that brings you Cyberpunk Librarian</segment>
		<segment id="83" parent="248" relname="same-unit">will be a new podcast about high adventure in deep space with librarians .</segment>
		<segment id="84" parent="211" relname="span">Intergalactic Librarian will be its own podcast .</segment>
		<segment id="85" parent="249" relname="joint-list">Look for that around the end of April or so .</segment>
		<segment id="86" parent="212" relname="adversative-concession">The first show will be the same as episode 30 with some edits ,</segment>
		<segment id="87" parent="213" relname="span">but that will not only serve to kick off the new podcast ,</segment>
		<segment id="88" parent="87" relname="explanation-justify">because after all , it 's nice to begin at the beginning ,</segment>
		<segment id="89" parent="153" relname="joint-list">but it 'll make sure that everything 's working ,</segment>
		<segment id="90" parent="153" relname="joint-list">all of the feeds are doing okay ,</segment>
		<segment id="91" parent="153" relname="joint-list">and that 's fine .</segment>
		<segment id="92" parent="167" relname="span">Also , there is a new look and feel for the Cyberpunk Librarian website .</segment>
		<segment id="93" parent="252" relname="span">I 'm looking to do some more content with a wider scope ,</segment>
		<segment id="94" parent="93" relname="causal-result">and hopefully the new look will showcase that a bit better .</segment>
		<segment id="95" parent="253" relname="span">Have a look</segment>
		<segment id="96" parent="95" relname="contingency-condition">if you 're interested .</segment>
		<segment id="97" parent="254" relname="span">cyberpunklibrarian.com .</segment>
		<segment id="98" parent="218" relname="span">And hey , finally , for those of you</segment>
		<segment id="99" parent="98" relname="elaboration-attribute">who do the Facebook thing ,</segment>
		<segment id="100" parent="221" relname="same-unit">dig on the new Cyberpunk Librarian page on Facebook .</segment>
		<segment id="101" parent="102" relname="causal-cause">I just created it .</segment>
		<segment id="102" parent="219" relname="span">So we 're kind of just getting started there .</segment>
		<segment id="103" parent="220" relname="span">But facebook.com/cyberpunklibrarian , you 'll find updates , new content , and all kinds of stuff there .</segment>
		<segment id="104" parent="255" relname="restatement-partial">Check it out , friends and listeners .</segment>
		<segment id="105" parent="262" relname="span">So , okay , housekeeping is over .</segment>
		<segment id="106" parent="257" relname="organization-preparation">See ,</segment>
		<segment id="107" parent="108" relname="attribution-positive">I told you</segment>
		<segment id="108" parent="257" relname="span">I would keep it short .</segment>
		<segment id="109" parent="263" relname="joint-list">Now then , we are going to talk about pictures</segment>
		<segment id="110" parent="263" relname="joint-list">and putting pictures on the web .</segment>
		<segment id="111" parent="263" relname="elaboration-additional">And specifically , we 're going to talk about putting pictures on your library websites and social media presences and all of that .</segment>
		<segment id="112" parent="169" relname="same-unit">Because</segment>
		<segment id="113" parent="258" relname="span">while you might use any image</segment>
		<segment id="114" parent="113" relname="elaboration-attribute">that you like</segment>
		<segment id="115" parent="259" relname="same-unit">on your personal Tumblr or blog ,</segment>
		<segment id="116" parent="222" relname="span">there are reasons</segment>
		<segment id="117" parent="116" relname="elaboration-attribute">you probably should n't do that with the library 's web presences .</segment>
		<segment id="118" parent="175" relname="span">After all , it 's piracy .</segment>
		<segment id="119" parent="226" relname="span">And piracy is bad , okay ?</segment>
		<segment id="120" parent="227" relname="joint-list">It 's freebooting another 's work</segment>
		<segment id="121" parent="227" relname="joint-list">and not giving them the credit .</segment>
		<segment id="122" parent="123" relname="attribution-positive">Unless the image specifically says</segment>
		<segment id="123" parent="264" relname="span">it 's free to use ,</segment>
		<segment id="124" parent="266" relname="span">always assume</segment>
		<segment id="125" parent="265" relname="span">that it 's not .</segment>
		<segment id="126" parent="180" relname="span">Second , it just looks bad for the library .</segment>
		<segment id="127" parent="267" relname="organization-phatic">You know ,</segment>
		<segment id="128" parent="267" relname="span">we 're supposed to be protecting and distributing content ,</segment>
		<segment id="129" parent="128" relname="adversative-antithesis">not ripping it off for our own websites .</segment>
		<segment id="130" parent="270" relname="same-unit">And</segment>
		<segment id="131" parent="132" relname="adversative-concession">while some collection development folks might bristle at this ,</segment>
		<segment id="132" parent="269" relname="span">your websites are part of your collection .</segment>
		<segment id="133" parent="270" relname="mode-manner">Just like your collection , your databases , your magazines , your public computers .</segment>
		<segment id="134" parent="174" relname="restatement-partial">These are all services you offer to your patrons .</segment>
		<segment id="135" parent="271" relname="joint-sequence">You would n't just pop down to B &amp; N</segment>
		<segment id="136" parent="271" relname="joint-sequence">and shoplift a book</segment>
		<segment id="137" parent="271" relname="topic-solutionhood">because a patron needed it .</segment>
		<segment id="138" parent="139" relname="attribution-positive">Or I hope</segment>
		<segment id="139" parent="272" relname="span">you would n't .</segment>
		<segment id="140" parent="273" relname="same-unit">Now ,</segment>
		<segment id="141" parent="228" relname="contingency-condition">if you would ,</segment>
		<segment id="142" parent="228" relname="span">you actually do have a sort of dedication</segment>
		<segment id="143" parent="142" relname="elaboration-attribute">that I admire ,</segment>
		<segment id="144" parent="273" relname="elaboration-additional">and we might discuss that in a later show .</segment>
		<segment id="145" parent="275" relname="span">However , your administrative folks probably wo n't think too highly of that idea ,</segment>
		<segment id="146" parent="277" relname="joint-sequence">so instead , you typically purchase the item legally</segment>
		<segment id="147" parent="277" relname="joint-sequence">and add it to your collection properly .</segment>
